 Small operations repository for the log retention job.
 
-`bin/archive-logs.sh SERVICE` packs the logs of one service from `logs/` into a dated
-tarball under `archives/`. It runs from cron on the log host every night.
+## Usage
 
-Archives are pruned by hand today.
+```
+bin/archive-logs.sh [--keep-days N] SERVICE [SERVICE...]
+```
+
+`bin/archive-logs.sh` packs the logs of each named service from `logs/` into a dated
+tarball (`SERVICE-YYYYMMDD.tar.gz`) under `archives/`. Several services can be given in
+one run. It runs from cron on the log host every night.
+
+- `--keep-days N` (or `--keep-days=N`): after all new archives are written, remove
+  archives in `archives/` older than N days. Only files named `*-YYYYMMDD.tar.gz` are
+  considered. Without this option nothing is removed.
+- On success it prints one summary line, for example
+  `archived 2 service(s): api web; pruned 3 archive(s) older than 30 day(s)`.
+- Service names are validated up front (letters, digits, `_`, `.`, `-`; no leading
+  separator) and each must have a directory under `logs/`. If any check fails, or any
+  archive fails to be written, the script exits non-zero and does not prune.
+
+Example:
+
+```
+bin/archive-logs.sh --keep-days 30 api web
+```
+
+Exit status: 0 success, 64 usage error or invalid input, 66 missing log directory.
+Paths are relative to the working directory, so run it from the repository root.
